From: szabo@netcom.com (Nick Szabo)
Date: Thu, 1 Dec 1994 15:34:05 -0800 (PST)
Subject: [#94-12-54] singularity

I should also point out that simply fitting a curve to data
points to find a trend, without determining the underlying cause 
of the trend and whether its continuation makes technological sense,
is nothing more than graphical numerology, a variant of numerology, 
astrology, and other superstitions which Extropians reject.

One of these kinds of projections was made in the 1950s.  It showed
that human travel speeds increasing exponentially, to the point where 
they would exceed the speed of light by the year 2000.  This curve
fit the data points up to that time quite well.   This piece of
graphical numerology misled a lot of people to predict that we would 
have Mars bases, O'Neill colonies, etc. by 1990.  Some even predicted 
interstellar travel, and FTL by 2000.    Unfortuneately, some
people who were involved in these projections have not learned
from their mistakes, and are again propagating mythologies 
to bedazzle the gullible.

